id":"04d1-a664-54dd-4ae1"},{"link_uuid":"59d2f0bf-a010-4e72-9e96-17c9a33df9a3","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"7901-f3bd-7db3-4405"},{"link_uuid":"0f4839b1-45ac-40b9-b7b5-fc33366d536f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"34ed-0955-45f1-405a"},{"link_uuid":"4f44906b-f512-4ccb-b5b6-29b92f7819f8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"72be-2810-40d3-4161"},{"link_uuid":"283d7440-c657-44bd-a98a-8790003d933f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"eae1-69f4-5726-4156"},{"link_uuid":"2ee08e8c-4c7f-414f-a909-5a88e44be195","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1df6-4175-af9e-4d6e"},{"link_uuid":"4465dacb-c600-4dac-91cc-a879be98fb4f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0ad7-4a32-4d11-4cc5"},{"link_uuid":"549d8c45-8c18-43d9-89e1-89e2a0c344a3","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8cf6-5201-0692-4c72"},{"link_uuid":"165be698-92ca-4b8f-980e-b4a651a1b362","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"eeff-ff24-8857-4c5d"},{"link_uuid":"5814674b-e649-42b1-80c8-5268f72d379c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"97eb-4313-03ee-4c59"},{"link_uuid":"cc58031e-db7d-4745-af93-c39b17ebe388","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1912-d0f1-915e-403b"},{"link_uuid":"1be77920-fbc7-4f03-b1a2-fefc05887096","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8da8-feb3-8d31-4e5d"},{"link_uuid":"adb9bec4-f9aa-46d2-ace6-ac0d9b7b4d66","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0977-8327-c37f-4a73"},{"link_uuid":"399a4cd4-d1e1-4e1b-b795-8d2bb9742505","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"9388-b823-9d42-46eb"},{"link_uuid":"0f88fd52-874f-4c3f-aedf-de6d4a91b98a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"88fb-2067-25b7-4b8a"},{"link_uuid":"a1ff3ce4-ec3b-4b93-a6a7-4774db927c73","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2ba3-1513-d168-44a7"},{"link_uuid":"0194efce-c0de-466f-b126-c04b8a05159c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"cb26-45ed-d6fd-4149"},{"link_uuid":"59d42642-aeab-4c2d-95cd-88971947cc0c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d347-c47a-1050-43bb"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/external cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/external/_live_llm.py:1-31, 54-59, 76-85, 140-151, 183-191` — Preserve provider resolution, provider-family mapping, credential rules, pinned-provider behavior, and region-not-credential distinction. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/_structured_matrix.py:1-17` — Preserve pure deterministic scoring/cap role and production-parser reuse. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/conftest.py:27-39, 63-69, 122-127, 147-155, 165-177, 196-201, 215-224, 233-238` — Preserve opt-in isolation, all-skip canary, marker mapping, live-model switch, committed prompt requirement, and plan fixture constraints. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_bedrock_cache_live.py:1-19` — Preserve opt-ins, AWS credential requirement, and real cache-observation contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_candidate_tracing_live.py:1-21` — Preserve real SDK parenting boundary, no-live-call fact, and optional-extra prerequisite. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py:1-22, 49-52, 149-154` — Preserve read-only live workload, pinned provider, evidence-response metric, and bounded banking oracle. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_completion_pass_live.py:1-12` — Preserve configured-provider readiness and per-criterion PASS evidence. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_deps_live.py:1-11` — Preserve live endpoint boundary, expected outcomes, and external opt-in. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_execution_mode_live.py:1-12` — Preserve live single-turn behavior and configured-provider gating. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_link_sync_live.py:1-22` — Preserve client-primitive scope, exact live shape, cleanup, and distinction from reconciler wiring. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_link_sync_roundtrip_live.py:1-38, 78-86, 303-309, 396-415, 444-456, 459-465, 477-488` — Preserve differ/apply boundary, absolute Blocks direction, delegation oracle, cleanup safety, and intentional inbound-apply exclusion. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_llm_trace.py:1-22, 131-135, 143-146` — Preserve real OTLP/Langfuse boundary, chosen review operation, and genuinely-new-trace oracle. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_model_requests_enabled.py:1-11` — Preserve external-tier reversal of the default model-request kill switch. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_provider_matrix_live.py:1-26, 56-67, 131-139` — Preserve realized-arm/provider checks, `cfg.model` second path, credential isolation, and Bedrock region requirements. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py:1-29, 69-79` — Preserve live operation coverage and Opus parameter-handling assertion. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_reconcile_live.py:1-20` — Preserve live preview boundary, opt-in, and expected plan shape. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_review_discovery_live.py:1-16` — Preserve live-provider discovery path and operator-attested opt-in. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/external/test_review_kernel_rules_live.py:1-21` — Preserve behavioral soft-rule cases and live-versus-deterministic boundary. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest --collect-only tests/external/_live_llm.py tests/external/_structured_matrix.py tests/external/conftest.py tests/external/test_bedrock_cache_live.py tests/external/test_candidate_tracing_live.py tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py tests/external/test_completion_pass_live.py tests/external/test_deps_live.py tests/external/test_execution_mode_live.py tests/external/test_link_sync_live.py tests/external/test_link_sync_roundtrip_live.py tests/external/test_llm_trace.py tests/external/test_model_requests_enabled.py tests/external/test_provider_matrix_live.py tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py tests/external/test_reconcile_live.py tests/external/test_review_discovery_live.py tests/external/test_review_kernel_rules_live.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/external/_live_llm.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/external/_structured_matrix.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/external/conftest.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/external/test_bedrock_cache_live.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/external/test_candidate_tracing_live.py","reason":"Conden